  "problem": "Let $c=\u27e8-2,1,5\u27e9$ and $d=\u27e84,0,-3\u27e9.$ Find the vector projection of $d$ onto $c.$\n\n${\\text{proj}}_{c}\\,d=\u27e8$\n{{field-1}}$,$\n{{field-2}}$,$\n{{field-3}}\n$\u27e9$",
  "worked_solution": "Using the formula for the vector projection, we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\text{proj}}_{c}\\,d & =\\frac{c\\cdot d}{c\\cdot c}c \\\\  & =\\frac{{c}_{x}{d}_{x}+{c}_{y}{d}_{y}+{c}_{z}{d}_{z}}{{c}_{x}^{2}+{c}_{y}^{2}+{c}_{z}^{2}}c \\\\  & =\\frac{(-2)\\cdot 4+1\\cdot 0+5\\cdot (-3)}{(-2)^{2}+{1}^{2}+{5}^{2}}c \\\\  & =\\frac{-8+0-15}{4+1+25}\u27e8-2,1,5\u27e9 \\\\  & =\\frac{-23}{30}\u27e8-2,1,5\u27e9 \\\\  & =\u27e8\\,\\frac{23}{15},-\\frac{23}{30},-\\frac{23}{6}\\,\u27e9.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
